Redis       → Key-value database
Cassandra   → Wide-column database
Neo4j       → Graph database 


5. SQL vs PostgreSQL
This is very important.
SQL= Structured Query Language
SQL is a language used to communicate with relational databases.
Example:SELECT * FROM students;
SQL itself is not a database.

PostgreSQL: PostgreSQL is a database management system that understands SQL. An open-source RDBMS that uses SQL
SQL
 ↓
Language used to communicate
 ↓
PostgreSQL
 ↓
Database Management System
 ↓
Database
So: SQL is a language, PostgreSQL is a database system.